course: dictionary
lesson: 382
title: Anywhere: any place at all
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Anywhere means in, at or to any place. «Sit anywhere you like» means you may pick any seat you want. The word stretches a little or a lot, depending on the sentence around it.
explain: Look for clues in questions and negatives. «Have you seen my bag anywhere?» asks about any place at all. «I can't find it anywhere» means it is in no place you have looked.
explain: Safety sentences use anywhere to make a rule strong. «Don't go anywhere with a stranger» means not to any place at all, not even a little way with them. Ask yourself: would any place fit here? If yes, anywhere is probably the right meaning.
fact: Anywhere means in, at or to any place.
fact: «Not anywhere» means in no place at all.
fact: In questions and negatives, anywhere means any place at all, as in «Have you seen my bag anywhere?»
fact: «Anywhere in the world» shows a very wide choice.
exercise: «Sit anywhere you like.» What does anywhere mean here? | Under the table | Only in the front row | *In any seat you choose
exercise: «I can't find it anywhere.» What does anywhere mean here? | In every place | In one place only | *In no place at all
exercise: In a maths problem, «anywhere from 5 to 10» means what? | The biggest number | *Any number in that range | Only 5 | Exactly 10
test: «Never go anywhere with someone you don't know.» What does anywhere mean in this safety rule? | Only at school | Slowly and carefully | *Any place at all | Near the front door
test: «The news shows frightening things from anywhere in the world, so a war can feel close.» What does «anywhere in the world» show? | Something in the sky | *A very wide choice | Just one country | A very small choice
exam: «The silk moth is not found anywhere in the wild.» What does this tell you? | Only in the forest | It is found very quickly | It is found in every forest | *It is found in no place in the wild
